// DISCOVERY: what runtimes does Dynatrace already see in this environment?
//
// Use this to size the .NET estate — but read the caveat before trusting a zero.
//
// CAVEAT, and it is the whole reason this project exists: process-group
// technology detection comes from OneAgent, and OneAgent's .NET detection on
// Alpine/musl is exactly the blind spot this pipeline fills. A musl .NET
// workload can legitimately report as LIBC, CONTAINERD, or nothing at all.
//
//   A zero here is NOT evidence that you have no .NET on Alpine.
//   It is weak evidence that you do.
//
// Confirm from the cluster side instead — see docs/DISCOVERY.md, "Count the pods".
//
// softwareTechnologies is an array of "type:X,edition:Y,version:Z" strings, so it
// needs expanding and splitting before it groups.
fetch dt.entity.process_group, from:-30d
| expand tech = softwareTechnologies
| fieldsAdd tech = splitString(tech, ",")[0]
| summarize process_groups = countDistinctExact(id), by:{tech}
| sort process_groups desc
